    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **James Wood** (75.37) anchor our offensive attack, representing our highest-ceiling plays. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and favorable dynamic platoon splits against Lugo, while **James Wood** capitalizes on an elite xwOBA (.422) and a favorable matchup against the hittable Ritchie. **Brice Turang** (75.06) also commands a top-tier slot; his ability to exploit Ure\u00f1a\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base opportunities, paired with a prime leadoff spot, makes him an essential start. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher test against the efficient Williams, his elite speed profile remains a category-anchor in our pursuit of stolen bases, even with the defensive warning regarding the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley** (46.04). Despite his pedigree, his recent projections were suppressed by a suboptimal order placement and a daunting matchup against Cavalli, ultimately falling short of the efficiency required to crack the starting nine. Meanwhile, **Cole Young** (43.76) remained on the outside looking in, despite his speed-friendly matchup against Bradley. Managers should keep a close eye on **Dalton Rushing** (41.25); his \"Lineup Pending\" status and a difficult L/L platoon disadvantage against Bennett leave him hovering near the roster\u2019s floor. We will proceed with caution regarding **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki**, as both carry wind-related risks that have tempered their base projections today.",
